{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Guides"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersets\/replacingaregistry"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"kind":"article","sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A registry is a list someone has to keep in step with the code: every analytics event type in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"array, every route in a table, every dependency registered in one function at startup. A new type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that isn’t added works everywhere except where the list is read, and nothing tells you. Moving the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"list onto LinkerSets takes four steps, and the list is deleted at the end.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Take an analytics library whose events are types conforming to ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsEvent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", collected by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hand so the library can validate their schemas at launch:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public protocol AnalyticsEvent {","    static var name: String { get }","}","","\/\/ Every module's events, listed by hand.","let allEvents: [any AnalyticsEvent.Type] = [","    Login.self,","    Logout.self,","    PurchaseCompleted.self,","]"]},{"anchor":"1-Give-the-library-a-macro","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"1. Give the library a macro"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Pick a kind (“evnt” is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0x6576_6E74"},{"text":", as ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","type":"reference"},{"text":" explains) and add a compiler plugin","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose macro requires the protocol, so its records hold ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"any AnalyticsEvent.Type"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func requiredConformance(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> TypeSyntax? {","        \"Analytics.AnalyticsEvent\"","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The library declares the macro and the kind, and re-exports LinkerSets for the expansion:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@_exported import LinkerSets","","extension LinkerSetKind {","    public static let events = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x6576_6E74)","}","","@attached(peer)","public macro Event() = #externalMacro(module: \"AnalyticsMacros\", type: \"EventMacro\")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The LinkerSetsMacroSupport module’s documentation has the package targets this needs."}]},{"anchor":"2-Read-the-set-beside-the-list","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"2. Read the set beside the list"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Before touching any event, read both and compare them, in a test or a debug build:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let discovered = LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values","let missing = allEvents.filter { listed in !discovered.contains { $0 == listed } }"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"missing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" starts as the whole list and shrinks as events are marked."}]},{"anchor":"3-Mark-each-event-where-its-declared","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"3. Mark each event where it’s declared"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@Event","struct Login: AnalyticsEvent {","    static let name = \"login\"","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event that doesn’t conform fails to compile. A generic event type, or one nested in a generic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type, is refused with a message, as "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse"},{"type":"text","text":" lists; such a type needs its concrete"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specializations listed by hand, or a concrete wrapper."}]},{"anchor":"4-Delete-the-list","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"4. Delete the list"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Once ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"missing"},{"text":" is empty, the library reads the set instead:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let allEvents = LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and the hand-written array goes. A new event is registered by writing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" on it, in whichever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module declares it."}]},{"anchor":"Other-registries","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Other registries"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The same steps fit any list whose entries can be declared as constants, functions or types:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorde